to work. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,490, up 0.7%. The NASDAQ composite finished at 25,374, up 1%. The TSX composite ended at 35,226, down 0.8%. 84% of S&amp;P 500 companies have beaten earnings estimates so far this season, which keeps the broader backdrop constructive even

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:29.100
while Canadian and US markets moved in opposite directions. Joint US Japan intervention to support the Yen stays active and adds FX volatility that any Canadian holding US assets needs to watch. Both the Bank of Canada and the Fed remain in holding patterns with the next decision still weeks away. 15-year fixed mortgage rates reached a one-year high this week, which raises refinancing costs directly for Canadian borrowers.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:53.300
Remember, we covered DAL about 23 days ago on record revenue and margin resilience. It closed down 1.41%, underscoring that even strong fundamentals can be overridden by sector rotation. With rates moving and volatility in FX, let us look at a strategy Canadian investors are using inside tax advantage to counts to generate income.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:02:20.280
Covered call ETFs sell call options against equity holdings to generate extra income while retaining ownership of the underlying shares. Two such vehicles now yield above 25%, which makes the income look attractive in a sideways or mildly bullish market. The sold calls cap upside participation and the underlying holdings can still decline sharply if sector rotation accelerates.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:44.760
Canadian investors can place this inside a TFSA by choosing a covered call ETF that tracks broad US or Canadian indices. They then monitor the call strike relative to the current price to see how much upside is being traded away. The approach has historically performed best in low volatility regimes where collected premiums exceed modest draw downs.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:03:09.560
It tends to lag in strong trending bull markets once the calls are exercised away. A same-day volume check above the 20-day average remains essential before treating any rebound in these ETFs as confirmed. The quiet change in risk comes from the fact that elevated yields now come with greater potential for the underlying assets to fall outside the covered range during sector rotation.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:36.140
Investors should therefore pair any allocation with the review of the ETFs holdings concentration and recent drawdown history before committing capital. Before placing any orders in these vehicles, it is worth understanding exactly how fills happen on volatile days. Imagine you place a market order for a US equity ETF right after the open on a day when mortgage rate data surprises the market.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:04:02.040
Your order fills at $48.72 even though the last quoted price on your screen was $48.55. The bid asks spread widened from $0.3 to $0.14 within the first 90 seconds as liquidity provider stepped back. Your market order crossed the wider ask while quoted depth on the bid dropped from 12,000 shares to fewer than 3,000.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:15.480
Professionals always check the depth of book and recent trade prints before sending a market order on news days. Retail investors who skip this step routinely pay 20-40 basis points more than necessary.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:29.800
The concrete misconception to avoid is assuming your brokerage's best execution guarantee eliminates slippage on fast moving names. Speaking of disciplined entry points, here is what we are watching this week in the practice portfolio.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:40.840
This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only. No real money is involved. Today's focus is monitoring race on the NYSE in the consumer sector.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:51.720
Ferrari reported a second quarter earnings miss on both top and bottom lines. We are waiting for post-earning stabilization above support rather than jumping in immediately.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:05:04.460
The defined trigger conditions are an RSI on the 14-day reading moving below 45 followed by a close above the 20-day moving average on volume at or above the 20-day average.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:16.380
The maximum acceptable loss remains 6% if the setup breaks below the most recent swing low. The target range sits at 3-6% over the 5-day window if support holds.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:24.100
Confidence sits at low because this remains a single factor setup with no confirming volume or sector rotation yet.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:35.440
This watch list approach demonstrates how to define precise trigger conditions before committing capital, turning an earnings miss into structured observation rather than an emotional reaction.

